    "title": "Testimony continues in Monongalia County murder trial - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Joey Rather ,\n5 hours ago\nMORGANTOWN, W.Va. (WBOY) — Day two of the murder trial for a man accused of killing his girlfriend and burying her in a shallow grave in Monongalia County in 2024 is in the books.\nThe day began with the jury hearing continued testimony from the West Virginia State Trooper in charge of the disappearance of Kimberly Osborne. The trooper told the court that surveillance video from the night of Osborne’s death showed a truck belonging to her boyfriend and the defendant, Joseph Nevera, leaving his cabin near where her body was eventually discovered, followed by another truck with its lights off.\n72 arrested; 2 missing kids recovered in West Virginia multi-agency operation The next witness was a crime scene specialist who told the court that no evidence of a struggle or homicide was found inside the cabin.\nJurors also heard from a witness who said they had seen bruises on Osborne, and also testified that she was a drug user.\nThe trial continues on Wednesday.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WBOY.com.",
    "summary": "MORGANTOWN, W.Va. (WBOY) — Day two of the murder trial for a man accused of killing his girlfriend and burying her in a shallow grave in Monongalia County in 2024 is in the books. The day began with the jury hearing continued testimony from the West Virginia State Trooper in charge of the disappearance of Kimberly Osborne.",
